      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $C$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has only $2$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(A)=2.$ As we can see, the matrix $B$ has exactly $3$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(B)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ only.\"",
