      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $5$ must have at least $5$ columns and at least $5$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the following matrices:\n\n- $B$ since it has only $2$ rows.\n\n- $C$ since it has only $3$ columns.\n\n- $D$ since it has only $3$ rows (and only $3$ columns).\n\nAlso, the matrix must have $5$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrix $A$ has exactly $5$ pivot columns, while the matrix $E$ has only $4$ pivot columns. So, $\\text{rank}(A)=5$ and $\\text{rank}(E)=4.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is the matrix $A.$",
