    "question": {
      ":question/id": "6c12399b-b8b5-5057-b7cd-8f5e04b79df0",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following matrices have a rank of $3?$\n\n$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 2 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 3 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,B=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 2 & 2 & 0 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1 & 4 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 3 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{bmatrix},\\,C=\\begin{bmatrix}1 & 0 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 2 & -3\\end{bmatrix}\n$$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "First, notice that a matrix of rank $3$ must have at least $3$ columns and at least $3$ rows. \nSo, we disregard the matrix $C$ since it has only $2$ rows. \n\nAlso, the matrix must have $3$ pivot columns. As we can see, the matrices  $A$ and $B$ have exactly $3$ pivot columns.  So, $\\text{rank}(A)=\\text{rank}(B)=3.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answers are \"$A$  and $B$ only.\"",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "8878bdd7-d505-58b9-9a39-1e8472c2ed41",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
